# Blocks rogue DHCP servers. Snooping drops any DHCP server reply arriving on an
# untrusted bridge port and logs it (topic bridge,warning) with the port and MAC.
# The router's own DHCP server is unaffected. Turns off bridge fast-path; 6.43+.
# Ports running a dhcp-client are trusted first, or the router's own lease dies
# at its next renewal. Trust any other legitimate uplink port by hand:
#   /interface bridge port set [find interface=<uplink>] trusted=yes
:foreach p in=[/interface bridge port find] do={:if ([:len [/ip dhcp-client find where interface=[/interface bridge port get $p interface]]]>0) do={/interface bridge port set $p trusted=yes}}
:foreach b in=[/interface bridge find] do={:local bn [/interface bridge get $b name]; :if ([:len [/ip dhcp-client find where interface=$bn]]=0) do={/interface bridge set $b dhcp-snooping=yes}}
